  "notes": "Chord-less maximal-minimalism: two Sound on Sound teardowns say there is **no chord instrument and no bass instrument besides the 808**, so `chords.impliedByRiff` is set and the sub carries both pitch and rhythm. That is why this is the only model on the bench whose `bassline.register` spans nineteen semitones with real passing tones — the 808 *is* the harmony instrument, and the research's three parallel 808 tracks, one transient-shaped and distorted \"so it almost functions like a bass\", are authored as `distortion: heavy` with `distortionWet` 0.7. The three parallel EQ'd hat tracks become one loud, dense stream: `fillDensity` 0.7 with lifted main and ghost velocities. Rolls are \"used as fills only\", which maps cleanly onto the split the engine already has — `hihat.rolls.freqPerBar` drops to 0.06 while `hihat.fill.prob` rises to 0.5. Melody is minor-pentatonic, monophonic and three pitches wide, with the mid-range deliberately vacated for the vocal. ⚠ INFERRED: the `i–VII` and `i–iv` families. The record has no chord instrument at all; those exist so the bass has more than one root to reach, and they are the first thing to delete if this ever sounds harmonised.",
